---
// Nooz product-page sections. Rendered into ProductLayout's slot (between the
// hero and the generic house sections), so the .feature/.feature-grid classes
// below come from ProductLayout's is:global stylesheet; only the screenshot
// frames are styled here.
//
// Every claim and number in this copy traces to one of the owner's ten app
// screenshots in /images/nooz/ (2026-07-29). Do not add capabilities that are
// not visible in a screenshot; the screenshots are the source of truth.
const IMG = (name) => `/images/nooz/${name}.jpg`
const W = 800
const H = 1757
---
<section class="feature">
  <div class="wrap feature-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="f-eyebrow">Contrast</div>
      <h2>You read 11 of the 652 it let through.</h2>
      <p>That line is a real ledger entry from the app. Contrast counts what flowed in, what the filter passed, and what you actually read, then names the widest gap by topic. Nooz shows you what you did not read instead of quietly deciding for you.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-visual">
      <img class="nz-shot" src={IMG('contrast-week')} width={W} height={H} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Nooz Contrast screen for one week: a dot-matrix world map, reach counts of 652 flowed, 652 through the filter, 11 read, and per-topic gap bars" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature reverse">
  <div class="wrap feature-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="f-eyebrow">The reader</div>
      <h2>Set like print, because news is reading.</h2>
      <p>Serif headlines on paper tones, photographs rendered as halftone dots, the reading time up front, and the source named on every story. Immersive mode hides the controls and leaves you a bare page.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-visual">
      <img class="nz-shot" src={IMG('reader')} width={W} height={H} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="A Nooz article with a serif headline, a halftone photograph, and a 6 minute reading time in the bottom toolbar" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature">
  <div class="wrap feature-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="f-eyebrow">Loaded language</div>
      <h2>Charged wording gets underlined, not deleted.</h2>
      <p>With the highlighter on, Nooz underlines loaded wording as you read. Tap a word to see why it was flagged, ask for a neutral rewrite, or dismiss the note. The article stays exactly as written; the call stays yours.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-visual">
      <img class="nz-shot" src={IMG('loaded-language')} width={W} height={H} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Nooz loaded-language sheet flagging the word threatened as a loaded verb, with buttons to suggest a neutral rewrite or dismiss" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature reverse">
  <div class="wrap feature-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="f-eyebrow">Bring your own model</div>
      <h2>Nooz Flash says nothing until you give it a voice.</h2>
      <p>The Flash briefing sits at the top of the feed and refuses to run until a model or API key is configured: set up an on-device model or connect a provider of your choosing. Nooz Cast reads an article aloud in a natural voice.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-visual">
      <img class="nz-shot" src={IMG('feed')} width={W} height={H} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Nooz feed with the Nooz Flash setup card, Nooz Cast, and serif headlines with halftone images" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature">
  <div class="wrap feature-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="f-eyebrow">Regions</div>
      <h2>Spin the globe, read a band of it.</h2>
      <p>The region picker is a globe: drag to spin, pinch to widen the band. Choose a slice like Europe &amp; Africa and the ring around it shows that band's topic mix, with Reset to Global one tap away.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-visual">
      <img class="nz-shot" src={IMG('region-globe')} width={W} height={H} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Nooz region picker: a dotted globe set to a Europe and Africa band with a topic-mix ring around it" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature reverse">
  <div class="wrap feature-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="f-eyebrow">Region &amp; topics</div>
      <h2>Numbers about your reading, for you alone.</h2>
      <p>Coverage, the breadth of the stream against the breadth of you, and each topic's over or under weight in what you read. When the mix changes, Nooz splits the why: how much because the stream shifted, how much because you chose differently.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-visual">
      <img class="nz-shot" src={IMG('region-topics')} width={W} height={H} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Nooz Region and Topics stats: coverage, breadth of the stream versus you, per-topic over and under weights, and what changed since the previous period" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature">
  <div class="wrap feature-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="f-eyebrow">Clippings</div>
      <h2>Saved stories become clippings, torn edges and all.</h2>
      <p>What you keep lands in a drawer of paper clippings: the masthead across the top, the topic in the corner, the date you clipped it. Share one onward or bookmark it for later.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-visual">
      <img class="nz-shot" src={IMG('clippings')} width={W} height={H} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Nooz clippings drawer: saved stories as torn paper cards with mastheads, topic tags, and clipped dates" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature reverse">
  <div class="wrap feature-grid">
    <div>
      <div class="f-eyebrow">Reading</div>
      <h2>Three faces, three sizes, and real paper grain.</h2>
      <p>Type comes in the house faces: Hyle Grotesk Classic, Hyle Grotesk Plus, and Hyle Print. Sizes are named Rice, Peanut, and Almond; paper grain runs from none to coarse; read articles turn grey or get struck through, your pick.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="feature-visual">
      <img class="nz-shot" src={IMG('reading-settings')} width={W} height={H} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Nooz reading settings: theme, the three Hyle fonts, text sizes named Rice, Peanut and Almond, paper grain, and immersive reading toggles" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="feature nz-days">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="nz-days-head">
      <div class="f-eyebrow">Day by day</div>
      <h2>The ledger works one day at a time, too.</h2>
      <p>Pick a single day or a range and Contrast redraws for just that window: what flowed, what got through, what you read.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="nz-pair">
      <img class="nz-shot" src={IMG('contrast-day')} width={W} height={H} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="Nooz Contrast for a single day, counting what flowed and what was read that day" />
      <img class="nz-shot" src={IMG('calendar')} width={W} height={H} loading="lazy" decoding="async" alt="The Nooz calendar sheet for picking a single day or a range" />
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .nz-shot {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 280px;
    height: auto;
    margin-inline: auto;
    border-radius: 24px;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    box-shadow: 0 30px 60px -26px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
  }
  .nz-days-head {
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 5vh;
  }
  .nz-days-head p {
    margin-inline: auto;
  }
  .nz-pair {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 5vw;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .nz-pair .nz-shot {
    margin-inline: 0;
    flex: 0 1 260px;
  }
</style>
